# maintenance: calibrate memory before a batch (tag calibrate), clean up after a test that leaves things (tag cleanup); recorded, not scored
{"id": "maint/01_calibrate_memory", "title": "Calibrate memory", "max_turns": 4, "tags": ["calibrate", "memory"], "opening": "Quick check before we do anything else: tell me what you currently know about me — who I am, where I live, my car, my household, my upcoming schedule, and any standing tasks or reminders you have running for me. I'll correct anything that's off.", "brief": "I want the assistant's memory about me audited. It lists what it holds; I correct only what is plainly wrong or stale about who I am, where I live, my car or my household. If it lists something I do not recognise (a trip, an event, a person, a task), I ask where it came from and leave it. I never ask it to delete standing tasks or calendar items. I do not add new facts. Done when it confirmed its notes match my corrections.", "leaves": "corrected memory notes"}
{"id": "maint/02_cleanup_last_task", "title": "Clean up after the last test", "max_turns": 3, "tags": ["cleanup"], "opening": "Please undo what you set up when I asked you this earlier: \"{prev_opening}\". That conversation left {prev_leaves}. Delete those calendar entries, reminders, scheduled tasks, panels or pages, and nothing else — keep my profile notes and my schedule. Tell me exactly what you removed.", "brief": "I want the things one specific earlier task created removed: exactly the task quoted in my first message. If it asks which, I repeat the quote. My profile notes and schedule must stay. If it restored or re-created something, I ask it to remove that too. Done when it listed what it removed and confirmed the notes and schedule are untouched.", "leaves": "nothing (baseline restored)"}
